WORKFLOW
1. Parse once; cache the whole object.
2. Define “today” = last timestamp in fintech_minutes.candles.t (fallback ⇢ hourly ⇢ daily).
3. Build:
   • snapshot = today’s O/H/L/C/V from the most-granular block.
   • forecast = next_prediction adjusted in step 4.
4. Adjust forecast:
   • Start from baseline.
   • Apply net upward/downward bias derived from:
       – active or completed candle patterns (target vs. stop)
       – distance to support/resistance across all three timeframes
       – short-term momentum signals (RSI extremes, EMA/MACD crosses)
       – trend strength (aggregate_indicator.trend.adx, trending)
   • Limit the explanation of this adjustment to ≤ 40 words.
5. Merge supports & resistances from minutes, hourly, daily; de-dupe within ±0.01; sort.
   Label levels below adjusted close S1…; above adjusted close R1….
6. Write the report exactly in this layout (plain text, no markdown):

<Symbol> Snapshot: O <>, H <>, L <>, C <>, V <>.

Forecast: expect O <>, H <>, L <>, C <>  (Δ explained in ≤40 words).

Key Levels: S1 <>, S2 <>, … | R1 <>, R2 <>, …

